In 1863, General Joseph Hooker sent more than 20,000 men with forces, artillery, and equipment from the Washington area to Chattanooga,

462
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:53,080
over 1,100 miles by railroad, in only 11 days.

463
00:34:53,081 --> 00:34:58,020
It was the longest, fastest troop movement in history until World War I.

464
00:34:58,980 --> 00:35:01,520
Military movers will return on Modern Marvelous.

465
00:35:04,800 --> 00:35:09,260
All modern military movers ultimately take their orders from a single command,

466
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:13,720
whose only responsibility is military transportation and logistics.

467
00:35:15,620 --> 00:35:20,940
At Scott Air Force Base in Illinois resides the United States Transportation Command,

468
00:35:20,941 --> 00:35:23,440
home of U.S. military logistics.

469
00:35:24,680 --> 00:35:26,760
It was a Civil War general who once said,

470
00:35:27,040 --> 00:35:30,600
victory goes to the side that gets there first with the most.

471
00:35:31,180 --> 00:35:33,440
And we're quite proud of U.S. Transportation Command

472
00:35:33,441 --> 00:35:36,060
and our components for all that they do

473
00:35:36,061 --> 00:35:39,560
because, in fact, if that's the litmus, the United States will win.

474
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:44,080
United States Transportation Command, or U.S. Transcom,

475
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:47,000
coordinates land, sea, and air transportation

476
00:35:47,001 --> 00:35:50,260
for the Department of Defense in times of war and peace.

477
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:54,500
The command consists of three military transportation components.

478
00:35:55,580 --> 00:35:57,240
The Air Force's Air Mobility Command,

479
00:35:57,840 --> 00:35:59,780
the Navy's Military Sealift Command,

480
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:02,800
and the Army's Military Traffic Management Command.

481
00:36:04,660 --> 00:36:06,300
On the eve of any war,

482
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:10,100
military experts have always considered three important aspects.

483
00:36:11,620 --> 00:36:13,500
One is battlefield tactics.

484
00:36:14,260 --> 00:36:15,480
Another is war strategy.

485
00:36:16,940 --> 00:36:18,720
The third is logistics,

486
00:36:18,721 --> 00:36:21,900
and to concerns arriving with troops and supply lines

487
00:36:21,901 --> 00:36:25,500
and sustaining them for the duration using military movers.

488
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:32,480
Logistics has always been the umbilical cord for any military action.

489
00:36:33,420 --> 00:36:38,380
It's providing the movement into a theater so that we can prosecute a war,

490
00:36:38,381 --> 00:36:40,820
so that we can provide sustainment.

491
00:36:40,980 --> 00:36:43,640
So if it moves in the United States military,

492
00:36:43,880 --> 00:36:47,080
it starts with and is moved by the United States Transportation Command.

493
00:36:48,720 --> 00:36:57,207
Every one of the Air Force's C-17s that flew resupply missions for Operation Enduring Freedom and Operation Iraqi Freedom was sent by U.S.

494
00:36:57,208 --> 00:36:57,908
Transcom.

495
00:36:58,320 --> 00:37:04,779
Every one of the Navy's roughly 100 LCACs running supplies from ship to shore is coordinated by U.S.

496
00:37:04,780 --> 00:37:05,480
Transcom.

497
00:37:06,020 --> 00:37:13,139
In fact, every military supply truck, cargo ship, and airplane full of equipment is overseen by U.S.

498
00:37:13,140 --> 00:37:13,840
Transcom.

499
00:37:13,841 --> 00:37:24,799
Transcom shipped more than 420,000 tons of supplies to aid more than 50,000 soldiers, coordinating thousands of cargo missions from bases in Europe and the United

500
00:37:24,800 --> 00:37:29,220
During the first year of Operation Enduring Freedom, U.S. States.

501
00:37:30,140 --> 00:37:38,899
We're a combination of not only the Air Force, the Army, the Marines, and the Navy, but the Coast Guard, our commercial contractors, and many of our civilian employees.

502
00:37:38,900 --> 00:37:42,080
It takes that whole team to be able to make Transcom operate.

503
00:37:42,081 --> 00:37:48,260
Bringing such diverse services and industries together has streamlined logistics for today's modern military.

504
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:54,000
But the concept of centralized military transportation has been around for a while.

505
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:57,440
Each branch, for example, has attempted internal coordination.

506
00:37:58,380 --> 00:38:03,240
The main lesson with each war, from the Revolutionary War up to World War I,

507
00:38:03,760 --> 00:38:08,100
is that transportation has to be centralized under one authority.

508
00:38:08,101 --> 00:38:13,200
And so it's in World War I that the American army, both in France and the United States,

509
00:38:13,600 --> 00:38:17,780
creates a singular office to control this, called the chief of transportation.

510
00:38:18,900 --> 00:38:22,340
But offices with limited power within one branch of the service

511
00:38:22,341 --> 00:38:26,700
were inadequate to effectively coordinate a multi-pronged force like the American military.

512
00:38:28,160 --> 00:38:32,060
Planners needed something bigger, answerable only to the Department of Defense.

513
00:38:32,660 --> 00:38:35,600
Before Transcom, the services did their own transportation.

514
00:38:36,300 --> 00:38:37,920
And they did it very poorly.

515
00:38:38,100 --> 00:38:43,340
The services are very reluctant to give up any of their transportation assets.

516
00:38:43,341 --> 00:38:50,980
So there is at least a dozen major attempts since the Second World War to unify transportation and Department of Defense in some way.

517
00:38:51,240 --> 00:38:54,340
They all failed for parochial service reasons.

518
00:38:55,560 --> 00:39:00,140
Then in 1978, the United States lost World War III.

519
00:39:01,400 --> 00:39:05,960
At least that's what happened in a top secret computer war game exercise called Nifty Nugget.

520
00:39:05,961 --> 00:39:12,160
With an enemy invading Europe, the Department of Defense simply could not reinforce its troops.

521
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:18,520
Shocked military leaders were forced to confront the need for a central logistics command.

522
00:39:19,760 --> 00:39:23,100
By 1987, all the pieces had fallen into place.

523
00:39:23,880 --> 00:39:30,280
Now Army, Navy and Air Force component leaders would work directly for the Secretary of Defense, reducing bureaucracy.

524
00:39:30,281 --> 00:39:33,055
When the Gulf War began in 1990, U.S.

525
00:39:33,056 --> 00:39:36,880
Transcom used the conflict to prove its efficiency,

526
00:39:36,881 --> 00:39:39,880
