00:40:16,821 --> 00:40:17,521
Command.

537
00:40:17,522 --> 00:40:22,720
We have multiple systems that are used to track planning, capacity and execution.

538
00:40:22,721 --> 00:40:25,960
So at any given time, we not only know what capability we have available, what capabilities

539
00:40:25,961 --> 00:40:28,371
being used, where it is in the world.

540
00:40:28,372 --> 00:40:32,020
Not only the lift platforms, but actually all the items,

541
00:40:32,340 --> 00:40:33,920
the right people, equipment, and supplies.

542
00:40:33,921 --> 00:40:36,140
We want to make sure that the right things get to the right

543
00:40:36,141 --> 00:40:38,327
place at the right time and the right quantity.

544
00:40:38,328 --> 00:40:40,420
There is an invisible marvel, and that is the

545
00:40:40,421 --> 00:40:48,600
information technology that supports the worldwide logistics to deliver as rapidly as possible

546
00:40:48,601 --> 00:40:54,680
the beans and bullets and supplies from the production facility racing across the world

547
00:40:54,681 --> 00:40:56,520
to get it to the folks who needs it.

548
00:40:57,420 --> 00:40:58,900
Borrowing from the private sector,

549
00:40:59,700 --> 00:41:03,560
U.S. Transcom can track equipment using radio frequency ID tags

550
00:41:03,561 --> 00:41:04,920
and computerized barcodes.

551
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:10,540
U.S. Transcom actually ships 80% of its supplies through the private sector.

552
00:41:13,300 --> 00:41:17,640
These companies might be transporting cargo or even soldiers for U.S. Transcom

553
00:41:17,641 --> 00:41:18,660
at any given time.

554
00:41:20,420 --> 00:41:22,520
We take a look at the requirement,

